      }
    ],
    "dv": {
      "description": "Two related dependent variables that operationalize the research question: (1) Reliance on social information (binary): whether the child chose a demonstrated option (majority or minority) versus the undemonstrated/unchosen option; (2) Preference for majority cues (binary among those who picked a demonstrated option): whether the child chose the majority option (versus the minority option). Both are returned so we can model (A) reliance on social information and (B) majority preference separately.",
      "columns": [
